// Generated once by nise; owned by this application. Nise will not overwrite it.

// This application is one statically built single-page application embedded
// in the Go binary. Both settings below are the whole of that contract, and
// both are inherited by every route unless a route deliberately overrides
// them.
//
//   - ssr = false. There is no Node server in the deployment: the Go binary
//     serves the built assets, so nothing can render a route per request.
//     Universal `load` functions therefore run only in the browser.
//
//   - prerender = false. adapter-static writes exactly one HTML document,
//     the `fallback` page named in svelte.config.js, and the Go server
//     serves it for every unmatched path. Prerendering here would instead
//     write one HTML file per crawled route, each a copy of the same empty
//     shell, and the fallback would then overwrite index.html at the end of
//     the build — the "Overwriting … with fallback page" warning adapter-
//     static prints when both apply to the same route.
//
// Protected routes are never prerendered, which this setting already
// guarantees for the whole tree. A genuinely public, content-shaped page may
// opt back in with `export const prerender = true` in its own +page.ts, but
// only if it needs no session: a prerendered page is written at build time
// and served identically to everyone.
export const ssr = false;
export const prerender = false;
